+## Sales import and variance
+
+`POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the header
+`ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` an ISO instant, `qty` a whole number)
+and answers `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }` (`dishes` is the number of dishes
+sold, the sum of `qty`) for what was imported. Tickets imported before are
+skipped. A bad row answers `bad_request`; an item running out answers
+`import_not_enough_stock` (409). Either way the message names the row
+(`row 2` is the first data row) and nothing is imported.
+
+`GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists
+`{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }` per item, where
+`theoretical` is the use from sales sold in those days (inclusive), `actual`
+is every `consume` movement in those days, and `difference` is
+`actual - theoretical`. Items where both are zero are left out.
